<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan flour group buys 61,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Taiwan flour group buys 61,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taiwan Flour Mills Association bought two shipments totalling 61,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat at tender on Tuesday, Taipei traders said.  </p>
<p>The two shipments were purchased FOB, traders said.</p>
<p>Suppliers Cargill, Agrex, Marubeni and Mitsui shared in the contracts for the two shipments.</p>
<p>Details of the tender are as follows:  </p>
<p> Supplier	Type   Tonnes  Delivery Period  Price</p>
<p>Shipment 1  Cargill	 DNS    18,100  Feb 15-Mar 5     $191.96</p>
<p> Agrex	   HRW    10,500			 $185.15</p>
<p> Marubeni	 WW     6,400			 $158.67</p>
<p>Shipment 2  Mitsui	  DNS    17,700  Feb 28-Mar 20    $187.60</p>
<p> Mitsui	  HRW     8,300			 $183.00</p>
<p>Freight was fixed at $21.5 a tonne for the first shipment and $22.75 per tonne for the second shipment.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
</text>
